The correct answer is __**Ctrl + H**__.

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/36f36cd5ece4186095afcf2ffbfb7b80cc04b6c2e3226e7477a419a9fbc96f85.png] **__Key Points__**

__

• The shortcut **Ctrl + H** is used in Microsoft Word to open the "Find and Replace" dialog box.

• This shortcut allows users to quickly find specific text within a document and replace it with different text.

• Using "Find and Replace" can save time and effort, especially in lengthy documents.

• This feature is particularly useful for making consistent changes throughout a document, such as correcting a typo or updating terminology.

• Other common shortcuts related to text editing include Ctrl + F (Find) and Ctrl + G (Go To).

 [IMAGE: https://cdn.repeatermock.com/tb/f13e2ad6582c16aa62a83672e2547ad20a01fddb61962a1acce42eb9a1a99caa.png] **Additional Information__**


• In addition to Ctrl + H, Microsoft Word offers various keyboard shortcuts to enhance productivity and efficiency.

• Keyboard shortcuts can be customized through the "Customize Keyboard" option in Word's settings.

• Other useful shortcuts include Ctrl + C (Copy), Ctrl + V (Paste), and Ctrl + Z (Undo).

• Learning and using keyboard shortcuts can significantly speed up the document editing process.

